---
description: Learning Anything — how to create, continue and validate courses in this repository
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is Learning Anything: you (the AI) research the subject on the web and write courses as JSON files in
`courses/<slug>/`; the local app only displays and grades them.

Read the root `AGENTS.md` before doing anything. Cursor and Codex read `AGENTS.md` directly; this file only exists so
Cursor never misses the rule.

The detailed steps are in the skills, which are plain Markdown files (read them even if your tool does not load them on
its own):

- `.claude/skills/create-course/SKILL.md` and `.claude/skills/create-course/reference/*.md` — create a course
- `.claude/skills/continue-course/SKILL.md` — write the next module and fix files with errors
- `.claude/skills/generate-videos/SKILL.md` — local voice and video
- `.claude/skills/answer-questions/SKILL.md` — answer questions about a lesson
- `.claude/skills/setup-machine/SKILL.md` — install and fix the optional parts (voice, Whisper, Ollama, focus mode)

Golden rule: after each file you write, run `npm run course:validate -- <slug>` and fix it until it passes.
